# RDNF match simplification: match arms are collected and their result types unioned.
# Before: infer_match returned Unknown for all match expressions.
# After: returns normalize_union(arm_types) |> simplify_type — precise and deduplicated.
# Both arms of [match result [Result.Ok v] v.value [Result.Error _] 0] are type-checked without error.
# The eval output verifies runtime correctness: Result.Ok arm executes and returns payload.
[result: [try [fn [] 42]]
 value: [match result
   [case [let p] [Result.Ok p]    p.value]
   [Result.Error _]:              0]]
=== out
Dict({"result": Variant(Result.Ok, Dict({"value": Int(42)})), "value": Int(42)})
